# The @qits scope lives in the platform's own npm repository, not on npmjs. Two lines, two
# services: the npmjs pull-through cache is qits-mirror's, the @qits scope is qits-artifacts'
# hosted registry. Both are the platform's public hosts — reachable from a workstation exactly
# as written here, with no in-network alias to swap in.
#
# Both hosts answer 401 without a credential. A workstation supplies one in ~/.npmrc, keyed by
# the scheme-less URL:
#   //mirror.qits.wohlben.eu/npm/npmjs/:_authToken=...
#   //registry.qits.wohlben.eu/artifacts/npm/npm/:_authToken=...
# In CI the release step writes the token itself; in an agent container the npm wrapper on PATH
# authenticates both hosts with the commissioned client pair. Nothing overrides or rewrites these
# two lines, and package-lock.json's `resolved` entries name only these two origins, committed as
# is and never retargeted.
registry=https://mirror.qits.wohlben.eu/npm/npmjs/
@qits:registry=https://registry.qits.wohlben.eu/artifacts/npm/npm/
